SporeApp.exe's expat 2.0.1 is the release with a few functions of xmltok_impl.c made external instead of static (or non-inlinable), so
that the slices can compile and match them one by one (found by byte-matching).  Each xmltok_impl.c instantiation
(normal_, little2_, big2_) in a slice is compiled from its own copy, xmltok_impl_<slice>_<n>.c.  tools/ci/setup_oss.sh
copies the release's lib/ to work/third_party/build/expat-retail, makes those copies and applies this patch; the expat
slices #include from there.  Everything else in the expat slices is the release, included unchanged.

